# codegraph

> A CLI-driven graph system for extracting, annotating, and analyzing codebase structure — designed for AI agents operating over large codebases.

---

## What is codegraph?

codegraph transforms a codebase into a structured knowledge graph that AI agents can query, annotate, and reason over. It answers the six questions an agent needs before it can improve any project:

| Question | Answered by |
|---|---|
| What exists in the code? | Graph_0 — structure |
| What does each component do? | Graph_1 — intent metadata |
| How does it currently behave? | Workflow — execution graph |
| How *should* it behave? | Suggested Workflow — architecture policy |
| What is broken or misaligned? | Tasks — agent work queue |
| What changed since last cycle? | Delta — incremental change log |

codegraph is an **analysis and mapping engine**. It does not repair code automatically. The agent reads the maps, reasons about architecture, and decides what to change. codegraph validates those changes and tracks what shifted.

