## Quick Start

```bash
pip install codegraph
cd your-project
codegraph build       # extract structure + build graphs
codegraph status      # see what needs attention
codegraph tasks       # generate agent work queue
```

From here, an agent reads `.codegraph/tasks/tasks.json`, produces `.codegraph/responses/agent_response.json`, and runs:

```bash
codegraph apply agent_response.json
codegraph delta
```

That's one full agent cycle.

---

## Example

Given a small trading project with three modules:

```
src/data.py   →   src/signal.py   →   src/trade.py
```

**Graph_0** (structure — auto-generated, do not edit):

```json
{ "id": "src/data.py::fetch_data",        "body_hash": "c72b4", "file": "src/data.py",   "type": "function", "line": 12 }
{ "id": "src/signal.py::generate_signal", "body_hash": "8f1c2", "file": "src/signal.py", "type": "function", "line": 34 }
{ "id": "src/trade.py::execute_order",    "body_hash": "3a9d1", "file": "src/trade.py",  "type": "function", "line": 21 }
```

**Graph_1** (metadata overlay — agent-annotated via CLI):

```json
{ "id": "src/data.py::fetch_data",        "intent": "fetch OHLCV market data from exchange REST API", "layer": 3 }
{ "id": "src/signal.py::generate_signal", "intent": "generate trading signal from price indicators",  "layer": 3 }
{ "id": "src/trade.py::execute_order",    "intent": "execute validated trade order on exchange",      "layer": 3 }
```

**Workflow** (behavior edges — auto-generated):

```
src/data.py::fetch_data
   ↓ (call, static)
src/signal.py::generate_signal
   ↓ (call, static)
src/trade.py::execute_order
```

`codegraph status` reports:

```
nodes:                    9
edges:                   12
nodes_missing_intent:     9
orphan_nodes:             0
workflow_edges:           6
```

After the agent runs `intent-apply`, `nodes_missing_intent` drops to 0 and the system is fully annotated.

